y and avoid the need for multiple joins."""'}], 'response': "Here's a summary of the provided SQL query rewrite strategies into one paragraph:\n\nThe given SQL query has been rewritten using various strategies. Some of these strategies include removing constant expressions from the ORDER BY clause, moving filter conditions to the ON clause of an INNER JOIN operation, simplifying constant arithmetic expressions and removing redundant CAST operations, applying the GROUP BY clause and aggregate functions to the data source, eliminating unnecessary WHERE clause conditions, rewriting multiple joins with the same table function into separate variables and then joining later, using derived tables or common table expressions (CTEs) to simplify the query, and performing calculations across rows using window functions. These strategies aim to improve query performance by reducing the size of datasets before joins occur, simplifying constant arithmetic expressions, eliminating unnecessary conditions, and optimizing join operations.", 'time': 1.8544137477874756}
